[
  {
    "id": 626635,
    "description": "<div style=\"padding: 30px 32px 30px 32px;\">After you have gone through the lab material, perform the following tasks on a lab machine. If you are connecting remotely, for load balancing reasons, it is a good idea to connect to the machine that is numbered your student id modulo 35. For example, if your student id modulo 35 gives 23, you can connect to ug23.cs.ualberta.ca.&nbsp;<br><br>\n<ul>\n<li>Create<span style=\"color: #42413b;\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\"><strong>&nbsp;readme.txt</strong>, a text file</span><span style=\"color: #42413b;\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\"> which will have your name, ccid, lab section and the following statement</span>\n<p>&nbsp;\"I declare that this is my work and I have not collaborated with anyone in doing this work.\"</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Create&nbsp;<strong>test1.txt,</strong>&nbsp;a text file with some (random) text.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Copy <strong>~drafiei/291/pub/</strong><strong>test2.txt </strong>to your current directory.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Create a tarball called <strong>lab1.tgz</strong> that includes the three files above (readme.txt, test1.txt, test2.txt) using the tar command with the z option.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Transfer lab1.tgz to your local machine and submit it here.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Your submission must include all required files in the right compressed format (as described).&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
    "due_at": "2025-09-13T05:59:59Z",
